 "notes": "GO's lane taxonomy is the base's with the Horn rules, which has the 14 subsumptions Konclude 0.7.0-1138 entails and the EL rules miss. The base passes the Horn memory budget on ore_ont_9663 and ore_ont_14817 and answers with the EL rules, so its taxonomy there equals el's, while the lane finishes with the Horn rules and adds subsumptions. Against Konclude's taxonomies in the development set comparison, the lane misses 33 of Konclude's subsumptions on ore_ont_9663 and 27 on ore_ont_14817, from axioms that are not Horn and stay left out, and gives none that Konclude does not. On ore_ont_9855 the el side leaves 109 axioms out, so its taxonomy differs. The ORE 2015 EL files and ChEBI lite have one taxonomy on all three sides. Conclusion counts on eight threads vary between rounds, and the taxonomies do not."
}
